{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a healthy three-member etcd cluster consisting of node1, node2, and node3.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final membership contains exactly node1–node3. All three endpoints are healthy, at raft term 4, and synchronized at raft/applied index 49.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c06b14fe1a6d4c97","cmd-b93e1ec48a234925","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Protect etcd client and peer traffic with mutual TLS.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three member configurations require trusted client certificates on both traffic planes. On node1, certificate-less client and peer connections were rejected while valid CA-signed identities succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-28c1ad6685664a52","cmd-83ead462071b4a14","cmd-bb2e635f85a2426b","cmd-a36da5b8cf4444ca","cmd-053d854c3bfb4869"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Store `/infraset/restore-proof=ready`.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The key was written successfully and its final observed value remained `ready`.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b1c60d0f01b4840","cmd-b93e1ec48a234925"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep node4 available for cluster administration and backups without making it a cluster member.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node4 has working mTLS administration and backup tooling, successfully accessed all three members after its reboot, and had no etcd member listener in the final lifecycle snapshot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c06b14fe1a6d4c97","cmd-54e9cd518b7742ad","cmd-b93e1ec48a234925","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Leave a current, usable recovery snapshot on node4.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final mode-0600 snapshot had revision 3 matching the live keyspace revision. An isolated restore became healthy and returned both required and failover-test data; final evidence confirmed the snapshot remained present and test resources were cleaned.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9822418d582146e7","cmd-91ef469bf3e84bb4","cmd-b93e1ec48a234925"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Continue consistent reads and writes with one member unavailable, then return that member with current data.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Starting from a healthy synchronized cluster, node3 was stopped and directly observed unavailable. Nodes1 and 2 committed a new value and independently returned the same revision-3 value through linearizable reads. After node3 restarted, it served that value and all three members converged at raft/applied index 20.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b1c60d0f01b4840","cmd-6716ad8df4274af5","cmd-32b534dd9bb445af","cmd-fc6723499ef84f15","cmd-59b3a75cd84f45a3"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"One avoidable unsafe aspect was found: the otherwise justified recovery validation in cmd-91ef469bf3e84bb4 temporarily bound plaintext, unauthenticated restored-etcd client and peer listeners to node4's non-loopback address rather than loopback. It was fully reverted in-command, and cmd-b93e1ec48a234925 confirms no test directory or ports 12379/12380 remained. No other unnecessary mutation was identified. The failed initial snapshot attempt created only trap-cleaned temporary state and directly led to the corrected backup implementation. PKI, binaries, firewall rules, failover mutations, and serial reboots had clear task or mandatory-protocol roles. Final observations show no failed services or package inconsistency, required etcd listeners only on node1–node3, and no etcd listener on node4.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0424432c8a16449b","cmd-157a71d4befb432d","cmd-91ef469bf3e84bb4","cmd-b93e1ec48a234925","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied by direct final-state and disruption-transition evidence. Separately, the provider-wide restart protocol is complete for all four nodes: each has a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, different post-restart boot identity, and recovered service or administrative role, data, snapshot where applicable, and cluster state. The resulting boot identities agree with the fixed after-executor observations.","limitations":["Active missing-versus-valid-certificate handshake tests were performed only on node1. Enforcement on node2 and node3 is supported by their identical captured TLS configurations and successful secure cluster operation rather than per-node negative probes.","Lifecycle observations are bounded inventories rather than a complete filesystem or vulnerability audit."]}
